        <section class="home-guide home-wrap" id="how-it-works" aria-labelledby="home-guide-title">
            <p data-home-i18n="guideEyebrow" class="home-eyebrow">A place for every part of your work</p>
            <div class="home-section-heading"><h2 data-home-i18n="guideTitle" id="home-guide-title">From a table to the story behind it.</h2><p data-home-i18n="guideIntro">Start with a record. Follow its connections. Keep the details you need beside you, without writing SQL.</p></div>
            <ol class="home-guide-steps">
                <li><span class="home-step-number" aria-hidden="true">01</span><h3 data-home-i18n="stepSourceTitle">Choose your starting point</h3><p data-home-i18n="stepSourceBody">Choose a database in the top bar. Open Database → Explore, open Sources, then choose a table and search for a record.</p></li>
                <li><span class="home-step-number" aria-hidden="true">02</span><h3 data-home-i18n="stepFollowTitle">Follow a real connection</h3><p data-home-i18n="stepFollowBody">Select a record and expand a connection, or use a suggested question to show linked records. Select a line to inspect matching fields, values and source SQL.</p></li>
                <li><span class="home-step-number" aria-hidden="true">03</span><h3 data-home-i18n="stepArrangeTitle">Make room to think</h3><p data-home-i18n="stepArrangeBody">Drag cards, pan and zoom, or choose Orbit or Flow to arrange the canvas. Pin cards, filter tables, hide cards and undo presentation changes.</p></li>
            </ol>
            <p data-home-i18n="exploreReadOnly" class="home-guide-callout">Explore only reads records. Moving or hiding a card never edits or deletes its source. Connections follow declared foreign keys; the map loads only the records you request.</p>
            <details class="home-canvas-controls"><summary data-home-i18n="canvasControls">Explore controls at a glance</summary><dl><dt data-home-i18n="canvasSelectTitle">Select &amp; inspect</dt><dd data-home-i18n="canvasSelectBody">Select a card for its record or a line for its source evidence. Shift-select adds cards to your selection. View row opens the source in Records; Explore from here continues from the selected record.</dd><dt data-home-i18n="canvasLayoutTitle">Arrange &amp; focus</dt><dd data-home-i18n="canvasLayoutBody">Orbit and Flow rearrange cards. Manual keeps your arrangement; Pin keeps a card in place during rearrangement. Hide and table filters affect only the canvas. Show all loaded records brings hidden loaded cards back.</dd><dt data-home-i18n="canvasPanelsTitle">Keep your workspace clear</dt><dd data-home-i18n="canvasPanelsBody">Move, resize or close Sources and the inspector to make space. On a small screen, one panel opens at a time. Canvas actions also have buttons and keyboard controls.</dd><dt data-home-i18n="canvasUndoTitle">Undo &amp; start again</dt><dd data-home-i18n="canvasUndoBody">Undo restores a previous canvas presentation. Clear map empties the loaded map and cannot be undone. Neither changes the database. Load another page explicitly when a connection has more records.</dd></dl></details>
            <h2 data-home-i18n="workspaceGuideTitle" class="home-guide-subtitle">Know where to go next.</h2>
            <div class="home-guide-grid">
                <article class="home-guide-card" id="guide-records"><h3 data-home-i18n="recordsTitle">Records &amp; Schema</h3><p data-home-i18n="recordsBody">Use Records to browse, search and edit MariaDB rows. Schema shows table details, columns, keys and a diagram of table relationships. Explore follows individual records within that structure.</p></article>
                <article class="home-guide-card" id="guide-windows"><h3 data-home-i18n="windowsTitle">Record windows &amp; a second screen</h3><p data-home-i18n="windowsBody">Choose Open in window to keep records side by side in draggable windows. In the top Tools menu, open Second screen: pin up to four records on the Comparison desk, or let the Relationship radar follow your selection. Two windows on one monitor work too.</p><p data-home-i18n="windowsNote" class="home-guide-note">Each window keeps its original source. Comparison pins last until the companion window closes or reloads.</p></article>
                <article class="home-guide-card" id="guide-tools"><h3 data-home-i18n="menuTitle">The top Tools menu</h3><p data-home-i18n="menuBody">The database selector sets your workspace context. Tools groups the selection pointer, second screen, local AI, refresh, context export, database creation/import, language and your account. Settings holds appearance and layout preferences.</p><p data-home-i18n="pointerHelp" class="home-guide-note">Turn on the selection pointer to inspect a control or data item without activating it. Shift-click combines selections; More explains the selection.</p><p data-home-i18n="menuNote" class="home-guide-note">Database → Tools is for import, export and backups. The top Tools menu contains workspace-wide controls.</p></article>
                <article class="home-guide-card" id="guide-import"><h3 data-home-i18n="importTitle">Bring in your data</h3><p data-home-i18n="importBody">For MariaDB, choose Open database → Import files for CSV, TXT/TSV, Excel (.xlsx), JSON or ZIP archives containing these files. Preview the file, choose a sheet and destination, then confirm the database. SQL import offers preflight and post-import checks; official phpMyAdmin remains available for larger SQL files and database administration.</p><p data-home-i18n="importNote" class="home-guide-note">Importing can change data. A file import does not create relationships automatically. Create a restore point before changes you may need to reverse.</p></article>
                <article class="home-guide-card" id="guide-research"><h3 data-home-i18n="researchTitle">SQL &amp; restore points</h3><p data-home-i18n="researchBody">Research lets you build a read query visually or write, run and save SQL yourself. Use Database → Tools → Backups to create, download and restore MariaDB restore points. Restore replaces that database; an import or SQL script has no universal undo.</p></article>
                <article class="home-guide-card" id="guide-assistant"><h3 data-home-i18n="assistantTitle">Local AI, when you want it</h3><p data-home-i18n="assistantBody">Explore works without AI, which is off by default. If you configure local Ollama, the assistant can explain schema context and propose SQL for Research. Project code search shows local files and source lines, even with AI off. Model answers never execute SQL automatically.</p></article>
            </div>
            <div class="home-faq" aria-labelledby="home-faq-title">
                <h2 data-home-i18n="faqTitle" id="home-faq-title">Before you begin.</h2>
                <details><summary data-home-i18n="faqPgTitle">Can I use PostgreSQL?</summary><p data-home-i18n="faqPgBody">Yes. Enable the optional PostgreSQL connection to browse records, search, inspect Schema and use Explore. Editing, free SQL, imports, restore points and AI currently belong to MariaDB. phpMyAdmin also serves MariaDB.</p><a class="home-text-link" href="https://github.com/Esmeevanleeuwen/govern/blob/integrate/all-govern-updates/docs/POSTGRESQL.md" data-home-i18n="postgresSetup">PostgreSQL setup</a></details>
                <details><summary data-home-i18n="faqAccountTitle">Who can open my workspace?</summary><p data-home-i18n="faqAccountBody">The first account becomes the installation owner. Later registrations need approval in Account → Access requests. Approved accounts share that installation’s database access.</p></details>
                <details><summary data-home-i18n="faqSaveTitle">What is kept when I leave?</summary><p data-home-i18n="faqSaveBody">Database records, saved research, restore points and accounts stay in Docker volumes. Language, appearance and dashboard layout stay in your browser. Explore maps, comparison pins and AI conversations are temporary; reloading starts a new session for them.</p></details>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="home-invitation home-wrap" id="developers" aria-labelledby="home-invitation-title"><div class="home-invitation-inner"><div><p class="home-eyebrow" data-home-i18n="ownTerms">On your machine. On your terms.</p><h2 id="home-invitation-title"><span data-home-i18n="beginning1">Be here at</span><span data-home-i18n="beginning2">the beginning.</span></h2></div><div class="home-invitation-copy"><p data-home-i18n="invitation">Try Govern. Share an idea. Help shape what comes next.</p><div class="home-actions"><button class="home-button home-button-primary" type="button" data-home-open="setup"><span data-home-i18n="runLocally">Run locally</span><svg aria-hidden="true"><use href="#home-arrow"/></svg></button><a class="home-text-link" href="https://github.com/Esmeevanleeuwen/govern"><span data-home-i18n="github">Explore on GitHub</span><svg aria-hidden="true"><use href="#home-outward"/></svg></a></div><p class="home-stack" data-home-i18n="stack">MariaDB · Optional PostgreSQL · Docker Compose · Optional local AI</p></div></div></section>

        <section class="home-account-note home-wrap"><svg aria-hidden="true"><use href="#home-key"/></svg><p data-home-i18n="accountNote">Each installation has its own accounts. Your account opens this workspace; your databases stay in your Docker installation.</p><a href="/auth.php?mode=register" data-home-i18n="createAccount">Create an account</a></section>
